Add `dub tree` command

Introduces a new `dub tree` command that prints the resolved dependency tree
of the current project, showing the selected version and the file system path
of every package. This makes it easy to tell path based packages (e.g.
referenced with a path dependency or registered with `dub add-path`) apart
from packages loaded from the package cache.

The `--invert=<package>` option prints the tree in reverse, listing all
packages that (directly or indirectly) depend on the given package instead.

All build related options (`-c`, `-b`, `--compiler`, `--arch`, ...) apply, so
that the printed tree matches the selected configuration, build type and
platform. Optional dependencies that were not selected are omitted, and
dependencies closing a cycle are marked with `(*)`.

Related: #937, #1064, #1065
